# Test / temp artifacts
/tmp/
*.tmp
# Runtime state jash writes into whatever directory it runs in. Without these,
# simply USING jash inside its own repo left untracked files behind, `git
# status --porcelain` reported the tree dirty, and the next build stamped the
# binary "<hash>+dirty" — a build marked dirty by the shell's own scratch files
# rather than by any source change. Tracked-file edits still mark it dirty,
# which is the signal that matters.
.jash_ratchet.key
.jash_chain.log
.jash_chain.log.*
.jash_session*


# scratchpad: local analysis clones, logs, backups — never tracked
scratchpad/claude-mem-analysis/
scratchpad/graphify-analysis/
scratchpad/*.log
scratchpad/*.bak

# ── W7: binarios NUNCA sao versionados ──────────────────────────────────────
# Custo ja pago por versiona-los: build-speed/jash-release e um Mach-O de macOS
# que tres gates preferiam a build/jash (morriam em rc 126), que produziu um
# "hang" fantasma investigado por semanas em test_jinv132 (nao travava — estava
# executando um Mach-O), e que o install_verify.sh chegou a um passo de copiar
# por cima de /usr/local/bin/jash, trocando o shell do sistema por um que o
# kernel recusa.
#
# Um .modjash embute um shared object NATIVO: o do mac e Mach-O e nao carrega no
# Linux ("invalid ELF header"), e vice-versa. Construa por host —
# modules/build_module.sh ja faz isso corretamente nos dois desde 2026-08-05.
build-*/
build_*/
/scratchpad/
/Docs/
/audits/
/patches-proposal/
/downloads/
c/compiler/benchmark
c/compiler/test_bytecode
plugins/**/*.so
